# Copy this file to `.denylist` (gitignored) and replace the placeholders
# with the terms that must never appear in a public commit: your company
# name and aliases, product names, employee names, account numbers, ticket
# prefixes. One term per line. Matching is case-insensitive substring.
#
#   cp .denylist.example .denylist
#
# Replace the two placeholders below rather than adding to them: while they
# stay in your .denylist the scanner flags this example file, which is the
# reminder that the list has not been edited yet.
#
# A tracked line that has to keep a listed term (or a typographic dash) can
# be allowlisted by ending it with the marker "# publish-ok". The scanner
# skips that line and reports the skip on stderr, so a bypass is never silent.
yourcompany.example
contoso
